Z||000000||redfiero||05-23-2000||08:46 PM||||Here shortly, I plan on rebuilding my brakes.  I have the Z24 wheels.  The calipers show very nicely.  What color should I paint them?  I will take some good before and afters.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-002f_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||05-23-2000||11:13 PM||||Hey man  Please don't paint your calipers.  Here is a cool idea get them polished.  They look good especially through rims that show it.  Once my fiero is finished I'll post some pictures and you'll see the difference.  Give me a week....<P>Later<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||05-23-2000||11:35 PM|||| I think if he wants to paint the calipers it is up to him. Dont tell him not too and what is with the "please"||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-23-2000||11:36 PM||||use a good epoxy paint or have them powder coated. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||frontal lobe||05-23-2000||11:45 PM||||IF I was going to paint the calipers, how about matching body paint color?<P>P.S.  Nice looking car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||05-24-2000||12:30 AM||||May I suggest: <BR>Yellow calipers look great with red.<BR>Use the high temp engine paint from most auto parts stores.<BR>Just follow the painting instructions.<BR>Then use a high temp clear coat.<BR>It is a great $5.00 modification.<P>Also an alternative for the polished look:<BR>Use the BBQ silver paint and then the high temp clear coat.||||reg||1
Z||000006||redfiero||05-24-2000||06:53 AM||||I thought about polishing them(or painting them silver) but I was afraid that the contrast wouldn't be enough for anyone to notice.  I think yellow would look good also.  Red may also blend too well with the car.  If they are a contrasting color, they will stand out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||05-24-2000||09:40 AM||||I thought of polishing mine, but living by the ocean leads me to believe there is a maintainance factor involved that might be too much of a hassle unless they are clear powder coated.  Oh well, that's down on the priority list. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||05-24-2000||09:47 AM||||I painted my GA calipers high-temp silver, so they wouldn't rust.  So far, they are doing their job, and they look pretty good.  Email me for up close pics if you want.<P>Maybe you can see them in this pic  <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/tracer/Fieroside1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/tracer/Fieroside1.jpg</A> <BR>Gee, wonder why I picked silver?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||05-24-2000||11:17 AM||||I'll probably paint mine when I go with the Beretta upgrade so they don't rust.  Wish they were made of something that could be polished, though.  Tom, good idea about power coating, but I would imagine that would get fairly expensive????  Might have to make a couple of calls when I get ready to do the deal.||||reg||1
Z||000010||HarryG||05-24-2000||12:16 PM||||Those wheels look great!<BR>What size tires are you running? ||||reg||5
Z||000011||lawrence||05-24-2000||12:41 PM||||I painted mine silver Rustoleum.  Just brushed it on since the surface of the casting is lumpy -- I didn't think it would be worth spraying.  This is what they look like:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/4/we.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/4/we.htm</A> <P>Paul Vargyas told me he was going to have the calipers of his Formula chromed, but I've never seen them.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fret Naught||05-24-2000||12:49 PM||||I think powder coating would be a good idea if you wanted to spend the money. I just put some wheels on, and I sand blasted and painted mine silver. I think they look real good, I also did my back plate. It was quick and in expensive. They just sort of blend in to the back ground and you don't see unless you look. My opinion is no matter what you do, it won't take long and they will be covered with brake dust and road grime anyway, so go with a low maintenance plan. I had polished calibers on my Harley, and they were a real pain to keep clean and looking good.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Uaana||05-24-2000||02:47 PM||||Heres a thought.<BR>For those of you interested in powder coating you could try the spray on stuff, as long as you have an old elec stove avail. the results are great and you cant beat the price, a used elec stove goes for about 25-50buck maybe less if you find one where only the oven works.<BR>just my 2c||||reg||1
Z||000014||redfiero||05-24-2000||03:09 PM||||HarryG,<P>Those are stock 16" wheels off of a Cavalier Z24.  I am running Eagle RSA's - 205/55/16's.||||reg||1
